    "category": "factual",
    "config": "vector",
    "answer": "According to \"PreGress: Ranking-Native Pre-training and Prompting for Graph Node Ranking\" (arXiv: 2608.09016v1), Section: experiments, the six public graphs used for inductive evaluation are:\n\n1. **soc-brightkite (BK)** \u2013 Social network ($|V| = 5.7 \\times 10^4$, $|E| = 2.1 \\times 10^5$, avg. deg. $7.0$)\n2. **socfb-OR (FB)** \u2013 Facebook network ($|V| = 6.3 \\times 10^4$, $|E| = 8.2 \\times 10^5$, avg. deg. $25.0$)\n3. **Flickr (FL)** \u2013 Image network ($|V| = 8.9 \\times 10^4$, $|E| = 8.9 \\times 10^5$, avg. deg. $10.0$)\n4. **youtube (YT)** \u2013 Video network ($|V| = 1.1 \\times 10^6$, $|E| = 3.0 \\times 10^6$, avg. deg. $5.3$)\n5. **web-spam (WS)** \u2013 Email network ($|V| = 4.8 \\times 10^3$, $|E| = 3.7 \\times 10^4$, avg. deg. $15.7$)\n6. **indochina-2004 (ID)** \u2013 Web network ($|V| = 1.1 \\times 10^4$, $|E| = 4.7 \\times 10^4$, avg. deg. $8.0$)\n\n*(Note: The paper also includes two user\u2013item bipartite graphs, **Yelp2018** and **MovieLens-100K**, in its total set of evaluation graphs).*",
    "retrieved_arxiv_ids": [
      "2608.08422v2",
      "2608.09016v1"
    ],
